#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175692 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176044 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf8d806a-b232-5ddd-ad0b-3af70f244194" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Congruent Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "bea49cf1-02d0-5aa0-9584-f2ea5a2eb30c" :question/math-academy-id "e-10584" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bdaee2dee98e41505c8a35c617a8f4fc035125ea8d504efecbe58afc9f7fd06c.png)\n\nIn the figure above,  $m \\angle CBD = 5x - 5^\\circ$ and $m \\angle ABD =2x + 10^\\circ .$ If $\\angle CBD \\cong \\angle ABD$, find $m \\angle ABC.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\angle CBD \\cong \\angle ABD$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CBD & =m∠ABD \\\\ 5x-{5}^{∘} & =2x+{10}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & =2x+{15}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & ={15}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={5}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $\\angle CBD$ is\n\n$$\nm \\angle CBD = 5x - 5^\\circ = 5 \\cdot 5^\\circ - 5^\\circ = 20^\\circ.\n$$\n\nSo, by the angle addition postulate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ABC & =m∠CBD+m∠ABD \\\\  & =m∠CBD+m∠CBD \\\\  & =2\\cdot m∠CBD \\\\  & =2\\cdot {20}^{∘} \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175761 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "beaec0ce-eca9-5e8c-903a-6bf152b37368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Angles Given Measures of Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "fbd1b514-35d8-54a1-91c1-168d330811e6" :question/math-academy-id "e-2605" :question/problem "From the information given below, find all of the angles that are congruent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={10}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠C & ={80}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠D & ={90}^{∘}-m∠C, \\\\ m∠E & =m∠B.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the measures of $\\angle D$ and $\\angle E\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠D & ={90}^{∘}-m∠C \\\\  & ={90}^{∘}-{80}^{∘} \\\\  & ={10}^{∘} \\\\  \\\\ m∠E & =m∠B \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={10}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={40}^{∘} \\\\ m∠C & ={80}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={10}^{∘} \\\\ m∠E & ={40}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have that $m \\angle A = m \\angle D$ and $m \\angle B = m \\angle E.$\n\nTherefore, $\\angle A \\cong \\angle D$ and $\\angle B \\cong \\angle E.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175762 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ca5614b-e796-5482-89c9-31410de84c33" :knowledge-point/title "Using Markings to Denote Congruent Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "bab99447-be6e-5ac0-906c-a9df9aa7f3f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-2606" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown below?\n\nI. $\\angle AOB\t\\cong \\angle COD$\n\nII. $\\angle COD \\cong \\angle BOC$\n\nIII. $m\\angle BOC = m\\angle DOE$\n\n![](images/7d/7d0729a38dd775d0f049656b23755ace3b42d07a4040004e14942c789544c30b.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $\\angle AOB$ and $\\angle COD$ are each marked with a single hash mark \"$|$,\" while\n\n- $\\angle BOC$ and $\\angle DOE$ are each marked with a double hash mark \"$||.$\"\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠COD \\\\ ∠BOC & ≅∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠COD \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo statements I and III are true, while statement II is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "beaec0ce-eca9-5e8c-903a-6bf152b37368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Angles Given Measures of Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1412c4fc-e940-5a13-938f-f42ffc7bae38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠1≅∠3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486639} {:answer/id #uuid "32063bf7-a5cd-521d-bf15-5b3735786623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠1≅∠2≅∠3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486701} {:answer/id #uuid "8a329f63-ac1e-52f9-9b8e-7b2a3fb444e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No congruent angles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486894} {:answer/id #uuid "8de4318a-2906-55e9-931e-cf86dcec431d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠2≅∠3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486901} {:answer/id #uuid "a01a68fa-e4f2-5768-b6b5-568cf27a978c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠1≅∠2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8de4318a-2906-55e9-931e-cf86dcec431d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠2≅∠3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486901} :answer-field/id #uuid "484e629d-dc7d-5e0c-9c4a-71a204024442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbfe98b2-d913-5b5f-9244-1e7d8b4485eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-103249" :question/problem "![](images/cb/cb2cda27c9ca2744c059279e853969858a7b3d1882cde343177badc7aa33145d.png)\n\nWhich of the angles shown above are congruent?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1 & ={25}^{∘} \\\\ m∠2 & ={75}^{∘} \\\\ m∠3 & ={75}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠2 & ≅∠3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ca5614b-e796-5482-89c9-31410de84c33" :knowledge-point/title "Using Markings to Denote Congruent Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "768b7745-c32f-54c2-a220-8d70a241d0a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486853} {:answer/id #uuid "9a0bec5f-4c14-5c93-a7d6-f8f9e52686fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486944} {:answer/id #uuid "c329693a-b5a2-5193-bff3-fcc7570fce63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487028} {:answer/id #uuid "d57dd289-7ae8-5e70-8539-2d1dccad2ded" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487062} {:answer/id #uuid "eed18f17-23d5-5bb5-8850-a0adb39c430e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "768b7745-c32f-54c2-a220-8d70a241d0a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486853} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee27135-1d65-5365-a4fe-10d624dd4bf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e51f05e0-1186-559b-935a-5d0ce775e04e" :question/math-academy-id "q-103278" :question/problem "![](images/62/62412006e358dd798b602547e22eb63c9c274b0d740df885e9c69a1af06bcb97.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown above?\n\nI. $m∠AOB=m∠COD$\n\nII. $m∠BOC=m∠EOF$\n\nIII. $m∠COD=m∠DOE$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $∠AOB$ and $∠EOF$ are marked with $|$,\n\n- $∠BOC$ and $∠DOE$ are marked with $||$, and\n\n- $∠COD$ is marked with $|||.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠EOF \\\\ ∠BOC & ≅∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠EOF \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠DOE.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the statements listed is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176098 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ca5614b-e796-5482-89c9-31410de84c33" :knowledge-point/title "Using Markings to Denote Congruent Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025b4786-1822-54f6-8a89-545a9e29ce30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486597} {:answer/id #uuid "08ed29c2-738e-5064-8c1e-443c10c88854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486612} {:answer/id #uuid "2e930325-1a99-5839-9271-dfd501f317a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486685} {:answer/id #uuid "3f59c7f0-25cf-5e54-909e-17e1f69d588c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486732} {:answer/id #uuid "93044a10-b554-519e-b7bf-4828f2f237be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "025b4786-1822-54f6-8a89-545a9e29ce30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486597} :answer-field/id #uuid "82dbe361-354a-56ad-a1e1-311213fab97b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "432febe7-1220-5082-90e3-bf3d1c64fe2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-103282" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6fe8fc042cc8d5645e9cf0df2fd297e018504c4248a45d348e4778a14caea9ca.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the angles shown above?\n\nI. $m∠AOB=m∠DOE$\n\nII. $m∠BOC=m∠COD$\n\nIII. $m∠BOC=m∠EOF$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that \n\n- $∠AOB$ and $∠DOE$ are marked with $|$,\n\n- $∠BOC$ and $∠COD$ are marked with $||$, and\n\n- $∠EOF$ is marked with $|||.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠AOB & ≅∠DOE \\\\ ∠BOC & ≅∠COD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠DOE \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠COD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo statements I and II are true, while statement III is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176044 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf8d806a-b232-5ddd-ad0b-3af70f244194" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Congruent Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f459c6b-e100-5735-b45e-47924f091ea7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{62}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486689} {:answer/id #uuid "581ed73c-cf1d-5c9e-8d9e-c9ed3dfd8693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486788} {:answer/id #uuid "a11247dd-8891-5b3a-b652-55fe89488a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{61}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486961} {:answer/id #uuid "a5899c01-ec5c-5efc-9fa4-246ca1a7e83d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{54}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486970} {:answer/id #uuid "c52c2501-6ddb-5f4c-9b08-d41101f8b031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "581ed73c-cf1d-5c9e-8d9e-c9ed3dfd8693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{58}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486788} :answer-field/id #uuid "aceb6eeb-1f00-5f1c-98f7-83af119247db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee0f2311-3092-5ace-8f43-a374a26eb15f" :question/math-academy-id "q-27332" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bdaee2dee98e41505c8a35c617a8f4fc035125ea8d504efecbe58afc9f7fd06c.png)\n\nIn the figure above,  $m∠CBD=3x+{5}^{∘}$ and $m∠ABD=6x-{19}^{∘}.$ If $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, find $m∠ABC.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CBD & =m∠ABD \\\\ 3x+{5}^{∘} & =6x-{19}^{∘} \\\\ 3x+{24}^{∘} & =6x \\\\ {24}^{∘} & =3x \\\\ {8}^{∘} & =x \\\\ x & ={8}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, by the angle addition postulate,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ABC & =m∠CBD+m∠ABD \\\\  & =2(m∠CBD) \\\\  & =2(3({8}^{∘})+{5}^{∘}) \\\\  & ={58}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176044 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf8d806a-b232-5ddd-ad0b-3af70f244194" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Problems Involving Congruent Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e3ddfe8-4646-5343-8f78-2cd78244074d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486727} {:answer/id #uuid "6bcabfca-0ad4-576f-b497-06484a7f0b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486829} {:answer/id #uuid "7c4292d3-7a67-5551-be24-06795728e304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{14}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486862} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad629dd-bda2-5cd2-80aa-e44785aca0d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{13}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486896} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b932ed-41fa-51ec-b39a-7c8a73e83033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{9}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e3ddfe8-4646-5343-8f78-2cd78244074d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{10}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486727} :answer-field/id #uuid "c61077a2-9a63-5c31-b3bc-86812d3d0fa7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38145db5-f11d-5939-a57b-880dc1abb8bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-27340" :question/problem "![](images/9c/9c14d7a4f9a460c3219cb457ff9f8ba8fb32a22101dfba3e0925aa8077b011cf.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $∠ABC$ is an angle and $D$ is a point in the interior of $∠ABC$ such that $m∠CBD=5x+{3}^{∘}.$ If $m∠ABC={106}^{∘}$ and $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "By the angle addition postulate,\n\n$$\nm∠ABC=m∠ABD+m∠CBD.\n$$\n\nSince $∠CBD≅∠ABD$, then we have $m∠CBD=m∠ABD.$  Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠ABC & =m∠ABD+m∠CBD \\\\  & =m∠CBD+m∠CBD \\\\  & =2m∠CBD.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that $m∠CBD=5x+{3}^{∘}$ and $m∠ABC={106}^{∘},$ we can solve for $x$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{106}^{∘} & =2(5x+3) \\\\ {106}^{∘} & =10x+{6}^{∘} \\\\ {100}^{∘} & =10x \\\\ {10}^{∘} & =x \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176097 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "beaec0ce-eca9-5e8c-903a-6bf152b37368" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Congruent Angles Given Measures of Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a47e6e-e748-5170-9990-f8983df2d694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠B≅∠E≅∠F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486662} {:answer/id #uuid "d00dc0e1-0d96-523c-8246-5417065296bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∠A≅∠D$ and $∠E≅∠F$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487050} {:answer/id #uuid "d4013e73-3d15-5194-8998-adb9155a3713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∠B≅∠E≅∠F$ and $∠C≅∠D$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487056} {:answer/id #uuid "ee75afad-a73a-54b9-8841-0058f005d40d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠E≅∠F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487102} {:answer/id #uuid "fa1625a5-d851-5bd9-bd6b-206acbfabb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∠B≅∠D$ and $∠E≅∠F$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21a47e6e-e748-5170-9990-f8983df2d694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∠B≅∠E≅∠F" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486662} :answer-field/id #uuid "41f591ce-644c-5a99-a40d-e21beea341a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5707b071-c7c6-5712-89ca-e66cbdfb1c32" :question/math-academy-id "q-52667" :question/problem "From the information given below, find all of the angles that are congruent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={30}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠B & ={150}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠C & ={180}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠D & ={180}^{∘}-m∠C, \\\\ m∠E & ={120}^{∘}+m∠A, \\\\ m∠F & =m∠E.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the measures of $∠D$, $∠E$ and $∠F:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠D & ={180}^{∘}-m∠C \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={0}^{∘} \\\\  \\\\ m∠E & ={120}^{∘}+m∠A \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}+{30}^{∘} \\\\  & ={150}^{∘} \\\\  \\\\ m∠F & =m∠E={150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ={30}^{∘} \\\\ m∠B & ={150}^{∘} \\\\ m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={0}^{∘} \\\\ m∠E & ={150}^{∘} \\\\ m∠F & ={150}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe have that $m∠B=m∠E=m∠F.$ Therefore, $∠B≅∠E≅∠F.$"}]}
